---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { operator } from '../legal';

const sections = [
  { id: 'about', title: 'About these terms' },
  { id: 'using-wovenleaf', title: 'Using Wovenleaf' },
  { id: 'your-files', title: 'Your files and copyright' },
  { id: 'goodreads', title: 'Goodreads imports' },
  { id: 'third-parties', title: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'backups', title: 'Your device and backups' },
  { id: 'availability', title: 'Availability and liability' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes and stopping use' },
  { id: 'rights', title: 'Your legal rights' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms for using Wovenleaf, including local imports, copyright responsibilities, backups, and third-party services."
  summary="A personal space for your reading. You choose the books and files you bring; you are responsible for having the right to use them."
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="about">
    <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms cover the Wovenleaf mobile app and this website. Wovenleaf is
      provided by {operator.name}, based in {operator.country} ("we", "us", or "our").
      "You" means the person using the app or website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please read these terms before using Wovenleaf. By using the app, you
      agree to them to the extent permitted by applicable law. If you do not
      agree, please stop using it. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains
      how information is handled; accepting these terms is not consent to unrelated
      data processing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="using-wovenleaf">
    <h2>2. Using Wovenleaf</h2>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf is a personal book tracker, EPUB reader, and audiobook player.
      It stores your library on your device and does not require a Wovenleaf
      account or provide a Wovenleaf cloud library. We grant you a personal,
      non-exclusive right to use the app in accordance with these terms and the
      rules of the app store through which you obtain it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You must be legally able to agree to these terms, or use Wovenleaf with
      the involvement of a parent or guardian where required. Use the app
      lawfully. Do not use it to infringe others’ rights, distribute unlawful
      content, or interfere with third-party services. Licenses for open-source
      components continue to govern those components.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-files">
    <h2>3. Your files and copyright</h2>
    <p>
      You choose the EPUBs, audiobooks, cover images, text, and other material
      you import. <strong
        >You are responsible for ensuring you have the legal right to import,
        copy, read, listen to, export, or share that material.</strong
      >
      That right may come from ownership of the relevant rights, a license, permission,
      the public domain, or an exception under applicable law. Having a copy of a
      file does not by itself give you every right to use it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf does not ask for proof of purchase or verify the ownership or
      licensing history of locally imported files. Technical acceptance of a
      file is not confirmation that its source or use is lawful. Responsibility
      for your sources and uses remains yours, including any infringement
      resulting from your actions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf does not provide a service for uploading, hosting, or
      distributing your imported book files. Importing a file does not transfer
      its ownership to us or give us a license to publish it. Wovenleaf does not
      grant rights in third-party books, remove digital rights management (DRM),
      or authorize bypassing access controls. Protected or incompatible files
      may not work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="goodreads">
    <h2>4. Goodreads imports</h2>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf reads Goodreads CSV exports you select or share with the app,
      prepares a local preview, and imports the changes you confirm. Goodreads
      sign-in and export creation take place on Goodreads’ own website;
      Wovenleaf does not need your Goodreads password or synchronize changes
      back to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Import only exports you are entitled to use. Review the preview and keep
      your original export: changes to the CSV format, incomplete records, or
      matching errors can affect the result. Missing covers may be looked up
      automatically through Open Library, as described in the privacy policy.
      Wovenleaf is independent of, and is not endorsed by, Goodreads.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-parties">
    <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Online book searches, ISBN lookups, and cover retrieval use Open Library,
      an Internet Archive project. Book information and images may be
      incomplete, incorrect, or unavailable. Their availability and any rights
      in their content are governed by the relevant providers and rights
      holders.
    </p>
    <p>
      App stores, websites you open, file providers you choose, and other
      third-party services have their own terms and privacy practices. Wovenleaf
      is not affiliated with those providers merely because it supports their
      exports, links to them, or uses their technology. Internet access and any
      charges from your network provider remain your responsibility.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="backups">
    <h2>6. Your device and backups</h2>
    <p>
      Keep your device secure and maintain copies of important files. Deleting
      app data, uninstalling the app, losing a device, or a storage failure can
      permanently remove your library and imported files. We do not hold a
      server copy from which we can restore them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Local recovery points are on the same device and are not a substitute for
      a separate backup. Review each export’s contents: some formats are not
      restorable, and book files or voice recordings may be excluded. Exports
      are not encrypted by Wovenleaf. You are responsible for where you save
      them and for having permission to share any included content.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="availability">
    <h2>7. Availability and liability</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to make Wovenleaf reliable, but cannot promise that every book or
      file will work, that third-party services will remain available, or that
      the app will always be free of errors. To the extent permitted by law, the
      app and website are provided "as is" and "as available", without
      additional warranties beyond those required by law.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, we are not responsible for losses caused
      by your unlawful use of imported content, failures of services outside our
      control, or indirect or unforeseeable losses. These terms do not exclude
      responsibility for our fraud, intentional misconduct, gross negligence,
      death or personal injury caused by negligence, or any other liability that
      cannot legally be limited. Your mandatory consumer rights, including
      applicable rights to remedies for defective digital content, remain
      intact.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>8. Changes and stopping use</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using Wovenleaf at any time. Export what you need before
      removing the app or its data. We may release updates or change features
      for compatibility, security, or other reasonable product needs, subject to
      any obligations we have under applicable law.
    </p>
    <p>
      If these terms change, we will publish the revised version here with a new
      effective date. For material changes, we will give any advance notice and
      obtain any agreement required by law. Changes do not remove rights or
      claims you already have.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2>9. Your legal rights</h2>
    <p>
      These terms do not deprive you of mandatory protections under the law
      where you live or prevent you from bringing a claim in any court available
      to you under applicable law. If a provision cannot be enforced, the
      remaining provisions continue to apply to the extent legally possible.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about these terms or concerns about Wovenleaf itself,
      contact {operator.name} at <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}
        >{operator.email}</a
      >. We cannot inspect, retrieve, or remotely remove files stored only on
      someone else’s device.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
